# ASG Documentation Standards

## Documentation hub reference

Keep your organization’s **documentation-hub** clone available (local path or Git
remote). Set **`$hub`** (PowerShell) to that repository root when copying templates.
From there open `templates/planning/`, `templates/diataxis/`, `docs/standards/`, and
`implementation/ai-rules/prompts/documentation-prompts.md` when writing or reviewing
documentation in this project.

## Repository layout (ASG scaffold)

- **Technical docs (Diataxis):** under **`docs/`** using **required subfolders** (see
  below). Do not place user-facing technical docs at repo root or under ad-hoc paths
  such as **`implementation/guides/`**.
- **Planning (Shape Up):** under **`about-this-repo/planning/`** (numbered docs and
  ADRs).
- **Working notes:** **`about-this-repo/.working/sessions/`** and
  **`about-this-repo/.working/audits/`** for drafts, sessions, and audits — not a
  substitute for **`docs/`**.

### Required `docs/` folders (mandatory)

Create and keep these directories so exports (for example SharePoint) preserve a
high-level Diataxis structure:

| Folder | Diataxis type | File naming |
| ------ | ------------- | ----------- |
| **`docs/tutorials/`** | Tutorial | `tutorial-[topic].md` |
| **`docs/how-to/`** | How-to | `how-to-[task].md` |
| **`docs/explanations/`** | Explanation | `explanation-[concept].md` |
| **`docs/reference/`** | Reference | `reference-[subject].md` |
| **`docs/runbooks/`** | Runbook | `runbook-[topic].md` |
| **`docs/standards/`** | Standards (org/project rules) | descriptive kebab or UPPERCASE names |

Add a **`docs/README.md`** index when the project has more than a few technical docs.
**documentation-hub** dogfoods this layout; see **`$hub/docs/`**.

Cursor Agent Skills for the same workflow live under **`.agents/skills/`** per
[Agent Skills](https://cursor.com/docs/skills).

